(A text read out of arguments's all or arguments's raw is a text wherever it is stored)
a list called kept is [].
a list called given is arguments's all.
a list called untouched is arguments's raw.
a text called word is element 1 of given.
append word to kept.
a text called 'raw word' is element 2 of untouched.
append 'raw word' to kept.
append element 1 of given to kept.
a text called opening is given's first.
append opening to kept.
For each 'given word' in given, append 'given word' to kept.
Print "kept: {kept}".

To 'keep the words'.
    a list called words is arguments's all.
    a list called held is [].
    a text called 'first word' is element 1 of words.
    append 'first word' to held.
    Print "held: {held}".

'keep the words'.
a list called grown is arguments's all.
append 5 to grown.
a list called copies is [].
For each item in grown, append item to copies.
Print "grown: {grown}, copies: {copies}".
a list called 'more given' is arguments's all.
append 8 to 'more given'.
For each word in 'more given', Print "{word}".
a list called 'more copies' is [].
For each word in 'more given', append word to 'more copies'.
Print "{more copies}".
